  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nThursday night opens with diminishing chances for rain as earlier\nstorms and outflow boundary mergers come to an end. The passage of\na weak shortwave trough in NW flow will see fit to bringing us\ndrier conditions for Friday, particularly as H5 heights begin\nrebounding to 592 dam through Saturday ahead of a sprawling high.\nThis spells hotter temperatures with record highs not out off the\ntable for Lubbock on Saturday until the high center sets its \nsights for the Deep South early next week. Southwest flow along \nthe back of the departing high will open our door to monsoonal \nmoisture and rain chances beginning Sunday evening and continuing \ndaily through the first half of the week. This theme receives \ngood support from the GEFS and EPS, both of which favor wetting \nrainfall for the Caprock as PWATs rise to 1/3\" to 3/4\" above \nnormal. The increased moisture and cloud cover will also help in \ncurbing highs into the lower 90s, although this is still several \ndegrees above normal.",
